issue_context.body:
I would expect that if a key gets downgraded internally, this is largely invisible to the user of that key. However this turns out not to be the case for the EVP_PKEY_public_check function:

Reproducer of the issue below:
````
#include <stdio.h>
#include <openssl/evp.h>
#include <openssl/rsa.h>

void check_key(EVP_PKEY *pkey)
{
    EVP_PKEY_CTX *pctx = EVP_PKEY_CTX_new(pkey, NULL);

    if (EVP_PKEY_public_check(pctx) > 0)
        printf("EVP_PKEY_public_check succeeded\n");
    else
        printf("EVP_PKEY_public_check failed\n");

    if (EVP_PKEY_check(pctx) > 0)
        printf("EVP_PKEY_check succeeded\n");
    else
        printf("EVP_PKEY_check failed\n");

    EVP_PKEY_CTX_free(pctx);
}

int main(void)
{
    RSA *r = RSA_new();

    EVP_PKEY *rsapkey = EVP_PKEY_new();
    EVP_PKEY_CTX *pctx;

    EVP_PKEY_assign_RSA(rsapkey, r);
    pctx = EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_name(NULL, "RSA", NULL);

    if (!EVP_PKEY_keygen_init(pctx)) {
        printf("Error initing keygen\n");
        return 1;
    }

    if (EVP_PKEY_CTX_set_rsa_keygen_bits(pctx, 2048) <= 0) {
        printf("Error setting RSA length\n");
        return 1;
    }
    if (!EVP_PKEY_keygen(pctx, &rsapkey)) {
        printf("Error generating key\n");
        return 1;
    }

    check_key(rsapkey);
    EVP_PKEY_get0(rsapkey);
    printf("After downgrading the key\n");
    check_key(rsapkey);

    EVP_PKEY_free(rsapkey);
    EVP_PKEY_CTX_free(pctx);
    return 0;
}
````
Running this code gives the following output:
````
EVP_PKEY_public_check succeeded
EVP_PKEY_check succeeded
After downgrading the key
EVP_PKEY_public_check failed
EVP_PKEY_check succeeded
````

So, prior to the downgrade calling `EVP_PKEY_public_check()` on the key succeeds. But after the downgrade it fails. The problem appears to be that downgrade completely removes any associated key manager, EVP_PKEY_public_check() does not attempt to find one if one does not already exist, and the RSA key type is not supported by EVP_PKEY_public_check() in the ameth/pmeth legacy codepath.
